        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugins): hide bundle commands when frontmatter uses on",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users shipping bundled Claude commands could set `disable-model-invocation: on` in command frontmatter and still have that command remain available for model invocation.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe bundle command loader now reuses the shared frontmatter boolean parser instead of maintaining a narrower local parser. This keeps the owner-local command-loading path aligned with the existing frontmatter contract without adding config, compatibility aliases, or broader plugin behavior changes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nBundle authors can use common boolean frontmatter values consistently: `on`, `yes`, and `1` disable model invocation, while `off`, `no`, and `0` leave commands available.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: bundle command loading excludes commands marked with `disable-model-invocation: on`, `yes`, and `1`, while preserving commands marked with `off`, `no`, and `0`.\n- Current-head proof at `ba873b39cf9ec34d3c59fd45536625aaffc01769`: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/plugins/bundle-commands.test.ts` passed with 1 test file.\n- Real temporary bundle proof at `ba873b39cf9ec34d3c59fd45536625aaffc01769`: `node --import tsx --input-type=module -` created a temporary Claude bundle with `plugins.load.paths` pointed at that bundle root, wrote `commands/disabled-on.md` and `commands/enabled-off.md`, then called the production `loadEnabledClaudeBundleCommands` path.\n\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"head\": \"ba873b39cf9ec34d3c59fd45536625aaffc01769\",\n    \"loadedCommandNames\": [\"enabled-off\"],\n    \"disabledOnPresent\": false,\n    \"enabledOffPresent\": true,\n    \"enabledOffSourceEndsWith\": true,\n    \"commandCount\": 1\n  }\n  ```\n\n- Committed diff hygiene: `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` passed.\n- Review proof: `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode commit --commit HEAD --engine codex` completed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Duplicate search: no open or closed PR/issue overlap for `disable-model-invocation frontmatter`, `parseFrontmatterBool disable-model-invocation`, or bundle command frontmatter boolean behavior; open self PRs had no same-root overlap.\n- Observed result: in the real temporary bundle proof, the final model-facing command list excludes the `on` command and retains the `off` command.",
